Subject: Record value types and numeric ranges per defining instruction

What this does
  Adds a per-instruction record to the AOT profile: for the value each
  instruction defines, the type set, the observed numeric range, whether a
  non-integral number and whether -0 were seen. It is written as a `P` line.

Why we need it
  Per-register type sets are the wrong granularity: the register allocator
  reuses a register for unrelated values, so a register's set is the union of
  all of them, and the compiler consumes types per defining instruction.

What it adds
  `JSAotProfPc` and the `P` line; `profmerge.py` merges the new line.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.

